## Should-fix dispositions
- #4 session_move tool: PRECISELY REGISTERED — the LLM-facing tool is NOT REGISTERED anywhere (engine/mod.rs:1571-1590 registers only session_rename + models; session_move_tool() at opencode_tools.rs:362 is dead code with an erroring body). The reposcan's "always errors" was the parked body; in fact the model never sees the tool (v2's registry DOES expose it — divergence). The user-facing session.move API + Worktrees dialog work (unchanged). Registered: wire = admit a Move inbox item engine-side (needs the destination location's services from the tool context) or delete the dead leaf.
- #5a prompt history/frecency/stash TUI persistence: NOT DONE (window) — stays registered (f1).
- #5b session-toggle persistence: GROUPING half LANDED (Settings row + ConfigSink.update_session_grouping → cli.json write-through, HttpConfigSink mirrors update_session_sidebar's shape). thinking/verbosity/scrollbar stay registered (no toggle state exists in the port to persist).

## Registered by this lane (new)
- OAuth-browser AUTO mode + command flows are wired (pending view + 500 ms status polls + esc-cancel), but the pending view's live output rows are the instructions field (command pending messages overwrite it) — a display approximation, functionally complete.
- Export options: thinking/tools toggles fixed at v2 defaults (rows describe them); DialogExportOptions' tab-cycling form is a 4-row select.
- open.menu's project half (cross-project switch) — pre-existing location-bound limitation.
- The default slash table (V2_SLASH/SLASH_COMMANDS) predates the session commands' wiring and omits /share /fork /compact /undo /redo /export (golden-corpus-pinned table; changing it needs a golden refresh). The command PALETTE reaches all of them; the PTY proof uses the palette path for share.

